## Lore

The Kittani are a brilliant, inventive and aggressive alien race who once conquered their own world and several others, until the Mechanoids overran their civilization in a seven year war. Splynncryth rescued a fleeing Kittani refugee fleet by opening a dimensional gateway, and the alliance struck then has lasted 38,000 years. The Kittani are now spread throughout the Splugorth empire, most of them in Lord Splynncryth''s domain. They admire the Splugorth as conquerors, are honored to serve them, and hope one day to be trusted to conquer whole worlds on their own. They are cheerful and high spirited, but cruel, and regard most other life forms as inferiors to be conquered and enslaved. They are fascinated by the union of magic and technology and long to learn the secrets of rune magic.

To a human a Kittani looks like an advanced ape: a gorilla-like face, a powerful body covered in short black hair, six-fingered hands and an enormous skull holding an equally large brain. They love advanced technology, and the deadlier the better, but also prize techno-wizard, bio-wizard and rune items and will use any weapon, primitive swords and clubs included, to prove themselves the best. Most avoid altering their own bodies, preferring robots and power armor, though they happily use bio-wizard microbes, parasites and symbiotes, especially on others.

Warriors typically fight in hand to hand: expert and wear mega-damage power armor into combat. They will often fight to the death rather than admit defeat.

## Field Mechanic/Scientist

The Kittani Field Mechanic/Scientist is the technical arm of the race: engineers, roboticists and computer specialists who build, repair and improve the Kittani''s weapons, robots and power armor in the field.

## GM Notes

Every known Kittani has sworn loyalty to the Splugorth. Traitors are hunted down and killed or captured, and capture means slavery, the gladiator arena or experimentation. Player characters should start at first or second level; NPCs average level 1D4+1. Alignment is any, but usually aberrant or miscreant.
